-- title:
--   Lower bound for supersingular places of X₁(M) in characteristic p
-- statement:
--   Let $p$ be a prime, let $M$ be a nonzero natural number with $5 \le M$ and $p \nmid M$, and let $\Omega$ be an algebraically closed field of characteristic $p$ (with decidable equality). Write $F =$ [`ModularCurve.x1FunctionFieldC`](def/ModularCurve_X1.html#L134) $\Omega\, M$ for the intermediate field of the Laurent series field $\Omega(\!(q)\!)$ obtained by adjoining to $\Omega$ the set `intFormRatiosC` $\Omega\,(\Gamma_1(M))$ of $q$-expansion ratios attached to $\Gamma_1(M)$, and let $\bar\jmath \in F$ be an element whose underlying Laurent series is [`ModularCurve.jqModC`](def/ModularCurve_JqCoeff.html#L15) $\Omega$, namely $q^{-1}$ times the image in $\Omega$ of the power series $E_4^3\eta^{-24}$. Then
--   $$(p-1)\cdot[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z) : \Gamma_1(M)\vee\langle -1\rangle] \;\le\; 12\cdot \#\{v\},$$
--   where $p-1$ is truncated subtraction, the index is that of the subgroup of $\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z)$ generated by $\Gamma_1(M)$ together with $-1$, and $v$ ranges over those places of $F$ over $\Omega$ — valuation subrings of $F$ that contain the image of $\Omega$, are proper, and are principal ideal rings — such that $\bar\jmath$ lies in the valuation subring of $v$ and its value $v(\bar\jmath)$, computed through the residue field via a section of $\Omega \to$ residue field, lies in [`ModularCurve.ssJSet`](def/ModularCurve_SupersingularModuli.html#L7) $p\,\Omega$, the set of $j \in \Omega$ such that every elliptic Weierstrass curve over $\Omega$ with $j$-invariant $j$ has no nonzero point annihilated by $p$.
--
--   This is the supersingular mass bound on the fine modular curve: the number of places of the function field of $X_1(M)_\Omega$ at which $\bar\jmath$ specialises to a supersingular $j$-invariant is at least $(p-1)[\mathrm{SL}_2(\mathbb Z):\pm\Gamma_1(M)]/12$, the inequality form of the Deuring–Eichler count. It feeds the genus computations for the base change of the $\Gamma_1(Mp)$ function field against the Igusa function field of $X_1(M)$, and a non-smoothness statement for the two-chart model of $X_1(Mp)$.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_sub_one_mul_index_gamma1_le_twelve_mul_natCard_evalAt_mem_ssJSet_x1FunctionFieldC.lean

